            <ArticleTitle>Asystole following left ventricular pacing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>815-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During biventricular ICD implantation, pacing the epicardial inferior posterior-lateral surface of the left ventricle via the coronary sinus produced asystole. The proposed mechanism is a Bezold-Jarisch reflex manifested by a drop in heart rate and blood pressure through direct C fiber stimulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
